IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-interpretation`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 7 Division 1 Subdivision (2): the penalties (section 137D) and the court's powers over non-compliance by substantial shareholders (section 137E).
-- Offence functions answer JUST TRUE when the elements are met and NOTHING otherwise at every split site (i) (the text says who is guilty, not who is innocent);
-- the bar on proceedings answers JUST FALSE outside its trigger (a bar is the provision's own question).

§ `s 137D: penalties under Subdivision (2)`

-- src:28523 | 137D.—(1) Any person who —
-- src:28525 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 135, 136(1)
-- src:28526 | or (2), 137, 137A or 137B; or
-- src:28528 | (b) in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or
-- src:28529 | 137B, provides any information which the person knows is
-- src:28530 | false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as
-- src:28531 | to whether it is,
-- src:28533 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall —
-- src:28535 | (c) in the case of an individual, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:28536 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:28537 | exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:28538 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:28539 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:28540 | after conviction; or
-- src:28542 | (d) in the case of a corporation, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:28543 | not exceeding $250,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:28544 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:28545 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:28546 | after conviction.
@ref s 137D(1) (src:28523-28546)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137D(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF ((`the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B" or "provides any information which the person knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

@ref s 137D(1) (the penalty) (src:28523-28546)
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 137D(1) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an individual`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        IF `the person is a corporation`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 0, FALSE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000, no imprisonment is stated, so 0; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an individual" and "in the case of a corporation" are the only cases the paragraphs name

-- src:28550 | (2) Any person who —
-- src:28552 | (a) contravenes section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B;
-- src:28553 | or
-- src:28555 | (b) in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or
-- src:28556 | 137B, provides any information which is false or
-- src:28557 | misleading in a material particular,
-- src:28559 | in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1) shall be guilty
-- src:28560 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:28561 | $25,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:28562 | exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:28563 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137D(2) (src:28550-28563)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137D(2) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B` OR `the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("contravenes section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B"), not that anyone else is innocent
        IF ((`the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (i) "in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1)": a case within subsection (1) is carved out of this one (a named complement)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 137D(2) (the penalty) (src:28550-28563)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137D(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $25,000 and a further fine not exceeding $2,500 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, 2500

-- src:28570 | (3) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:28571 | offence under this section after ––
-- src:28573 | (a) a court has made an order against the person for the
-- src:28574 | payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD in respect
-- src:28575 | of the same contravention; or
-- src:28577 | (b) the person has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:28578 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:28579 | civil penalty under section 137ZD(4), in respect of the
-- src:28580 | same contravention.
@ref s 137D(3) (src:28570-28580)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention?
    `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137D(3) no proceedings may be instituted for an offence under section 137D` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` OR `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an offence under this section after"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (b): the bar is limited by its own wording ("after"); outside the limit the other reading is NOTHING.

§ `s 137E: powers of the court with respect to non-compliance by substantial shareholders`

-- The orders of subsection (1), paragraphs (a) to (i). The kind matters in subsection (6), which carves out "an order restraining the exercise of voting rights" (paragraph (c));
-- fork register A7: paragraph (h), an order that the exercise of voting or other rights be disregarded, is not read as an order restraining their exercise.
DECLARE `s 137E(1) kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `s 137E(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial shareholder from disposing of any interest in the shares`
    `s 137E(1)(b) an order restraining the holder or the person entitled to be the holder of the shares from disposing of any interest in them`
    `s 137E(1)(c) an order restraining the exercise by any person of any voting or other rights attached to a share`
    `s 137E(1)(d) an order directing the corporation not to make payment, or to defer making payment, of any sum due in respect of a share`
    `s 137E(1)(e) an order directing the sale of any or all of the shares`
    `s 137E(1)(f) an order directing the corporation not to register the transfer or transmission of shares`
    `s 137E(1)(g) an order directing the Depository or any depository corporation not to register the transfer or transmission of shares`
    `s 137E(1)(h) an order that any exercise of the voting or other rights attached to shares be disregarded`
    `s 137E(1)(i) an order directing the corporation or any other person to do or refrain from doing an act to secure compliance with another order`

-- The court "may, on the application of the Authority": a "Where ..." condition and an application, on a function named for a power. SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork line B3:
-- the grant limit of the ruling of 2026-11-12 answers NOTHING when the gate fails; the periods ruling (b) would answer JUST FALSE. The same answer serves every paragraph (a) to (i).
-- src:28587 | 137E.—(1) Where a person is or has been a substantial shareholder
-- src:28588 | in a corporation and has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or
-- src:28589 | 137, a court may, on the application of the Authority, whether or not
-- src:28590 | that failure still continues, make one or more of the following orders:
@ref s 137E(1) (src:28587-28590)
GIVEN
    `the person is or has been a substantial shareholder in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person, or has the person been, a substantial shareholder in the corporation?
    `the person has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 (whether or not that failure still continues)?
    `the Authority has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority applied to the court for an order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137E(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the person is or has been a substantial shareholder in the corporation` AND `the person has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137` AND `the Authority has applied to the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "Where a person is or has been a substantial shareholder in a corporation and has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137, a court may, on the application of the Authority"

-- src:28640 | (2) Any order made under this section may include such ancillary or
-- src:28641 | consequential provisions as the court thinks just.
@ref s 137E(2) (src:28640-28641)
GIVEN
    `an order has been made by the court under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137E(2) the order may include ancillary or consequential provisions the court thinks just` MEANS
    IF `an order has been made by the court under the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any order made under this section may include such ancillary or consequential provisions as the court thinks just"

-- Subsection (3): a sale order may carry a condition against a sale to a person who is, or would become, a substantial shareholder.
-- src:28645 | (3) An order made under this section directing the sale of any share
-- src:28646 | may provide that the sale is to be made within such time and subject
-- src:28647 | to such conditions (if any) as the court thinks fit, including, if the
-- src:28648 | court thinks fit, a condition that the sale must not be made to a person
-- src:28649 | who is, or, as a result of the sale, would become a substantial
-- src:28650 | shareholder in the corporation.
@ref s 137E(3) (src:28645-28650)
GIVEN
    `an order directing the sale of a share has been made under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order directing the sale of a share?
    `the court has made it a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or would become, a substantial shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made it a condition of the sale that it must not be made to a person who is, or as a result would become, a substantial shareholder in the corporation?
    `the buyer is, or as a result of the sale would become, a substantial shareholder in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the buyer, or would the buyer as a result of the sale become, a substantial shareholder in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137E(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` MEANS
    IF `an order directing the sale of a share has been made under the section` AND `the court has made it a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or would become, a substantial shareholder` AND `the buyer is, or as a result of the sale would become, a substantial shareholder in the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "including, if the court thinks fit, a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or, as a result of the sale, would become a substantial shareholder in the corporation"

-- Subsection (4): where a share is not sold, the Authority may apply for directions (SPLIT-SITE (ii): a "Where" gate on a function named for a power; fork line B4).
-- src:28654 | (4) Where a share is not sold in accordance with an order of the
-- src:28655 | court under this section, the Authority may apply to the court for
-- src:28656 | directions, including directions as to who the unsold share is to vest
-- src:28657 | in.
@ref s 137E(4) (src:28654-28657)
GIVEN
    `a share has not been sold in accordance with an order of the court under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a share not been sold in accordance with an order of the court under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137E(4) the Authority may apply to the court for directions on the unsold share` MEANS
    IF `a share has not been sold in accordance with an order of the court under the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "Where a share is not sold in accordance with an order of the court under this section, the Authority may apply to the court for directions"

-- src:28661 | (5) The court, before making an order under this section and in
-- src:28662 | determining the terms of such an order, is to satisfy itself, so far as it
-- src:28663 | can reasonably do so, that the order would not unfairly prejudice any
-- src:28664 | person.
@ref s 137E(5) (src:28661-28664)
GIVEN
    `the court is about to make an order under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court about to make an order under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137E(5) the court must first satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person` MEANS
    IF `the court is about to make an order under the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before making an order under this section and in determining the terms of such an order"

-- Subsection (6): the bar. The court "is not to make an order ... other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights, if it is satisfied" of (a) inadvertence, mistake or unawareness
-- and (b) that the failure ought to be excused. JUST TRUE is "barred". Outside the carve-out or the condition the answer is JUST FALSE ("the bar does not apply"): a bar is the provision's own question
-- (ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2); the other reading, NOTHING, is listed in NOTES.md (marginal reading (b)). "(other than X)" is a site decided on its own words: fork line B5.
-- src:28671 | (6) The court is not to make an order under this section, other than
-- src:28672 | an order restraining the exercise of voting rights, if it is satisfied —
-- src:28674 | (a) that the failure of the person who is or has been a
-- src:28675 | substantial shareholder to comply as mentioned in
-- src:28676 | subsection (1) was due to the person’s inadvertence or
-- src:28677 | mistake or to the person not being aware of a relevant fact
-- src:28678 | or occurrence; and
-- src:28680 | (b) that in all the circumstances, the failure ought to be
-- src:28681 | excused.
@ref s 137E(6) (src:28671-28681)
GIVEN
    `the kind of order` IS A `s 137E(1) kind of order` @desc Which kind of order is it (restrain disposal, restrain voting or other rights, withhold payment, direct a sale, stop registration of a transfer, disregard votes, or secure compliance)?
    `the court is satisfied that the failure was due to inadvertence or mistake or to not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the failure to comply was due to the person's inadvertence or mistake or to the person not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence?
    `the court is satisfied that in all the circumstances the failure ought to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that in all the circumstances the failure ought to be excused?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137E(6) the court is not to make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of order` EQUALS `s 137E(1)(c) an order restraining the exercise by any person of any voting or other rights attached to a share`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights"
        IF `the court is satisfied that the failure was due to inadvertence or mistake or to not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence` AND `the court is satisfied that in all the circumstances the failure ought to be excused`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is satisfied — (a) that the failure of the person who is or has been a substantial shareholder to comply as mentioned in subsection (1) was due to the person's inadvertence or mistake or to the person not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence; and (b) that in all the circumstances, the failure ought to be excused"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the bar is introduced with "if"; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no. The other reading is NOTHING.

