DECLARE `s 137E action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137E contravene an order of the court made under the section`

-- src:28697 | (9) Any person who contravenes an order made under this section
-- src:28698 | that is applicable to the person shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:28699 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the
-- src:28700 | case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000
-- src:28701 | for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:28702 | conviction.
@ref s 137E(9) (the prohibition as a regulative rule) (src:28697-28702)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137E action`
`s 137E(9) the person shall not contravene an order of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    SHANT `s 137E contravene an order of the court made under the section`
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "contravened an order of the court made under section 137E that is applicable to the person (section 137E(9))"

-- Subsection (10): contempt is untouched.
-- src:28706 | (10) Subsection (9) does not affect the powers of the court in
-- src:28707 | relation to the punishment of contempt of the court.
@ref s 137E(10) (src:28706-28707)
